course: dictionary
lesson: 8617
title: Screenshots: a picture of the screen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A screenshot is a picture of what is showing on a screen at that moment. The screen can be a computer, tablet or phone. To screenshot means to take that picture. Context shows this: in a computing lesson you might «take a screenshot» to show the steps of your work, so it is a picture of your screen, not a real screen.
explain: The words around a word are its context, and they leave clues. «Send a screenshot» tells you that a screenshot is something you can send, like a picture. Swap in your meaning: «send a picture of the screen» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Online safety adds an important clue. Anything you send can be screenshotted and shared, so it may never go away. If someone is mean to you, do not reply. Instead, save a screenshot, tell a trusted adult, then block and report.
fact: A screenshot is a picture of the screen at one moment.
fact: To screenshot means to take that picture.
fact: Anything you send can be screenshotted and shared by someone else, so it may never fully go away.
fact: «Save a screenshot» of an upsetting message, then show a trusted adult.
fact: Telling a trusted adult about an upsetting message is not getting into trouble.
exercise: What is a screenshot? | A film recorded from a camera | A printed photo of a keyboard | *A picture of what is showing on a screen at that moment
exercise: If someone is mean to you in a game chat, what should you do with a screenshot? | Reply with a meaner message | *Show it to a trusted adult | Post it so everyone can laugh | Keep it secret and never tell anyone
exercise: Ella's teacher says, «Send a screenshot of your code.» What does screenshot mean here? | A quiet game | A broken screen | *A picture of the screen
test: Why might a message you send never go away? | Because screens never switch off | *Because anyone you send it to can screenshot it and share it | Because messages cannot be deleted from a phone | Because teachers keep every message in a book
test: Which sentence uses screenshot as a verb, meaning to take a picture? | *She screenshotted the error to show her teacher | The screenshot was blue | A screenshot is a picture | The screen was broken
exam: Ben sees a nasty message in a game chat. What is the best first step? | Reply with a meaner message | *Save a screenshot and tell a trusted adult | Delete it, say nothing and hope it stops | Post it so others can laugh at the sender
